      children: "A and B are white crystalline substances. Both are highly soluble in water and can be moderately heated (up to 200 °C) without change but both decompose at higher temperatures. If an aqueous solution of 20.00 g A (which is slightly basic, pH ≈ 8.5–9) is added to an aqueous solution of 11.52 g B (which is slightly acidic, pH ≈ 4.5–5) a white precipitate C forms that weighs 20.35 g after filtering, washing and drying. The filtrate is essentially neutral and gives a brown colour reaction with an acidified KI solution. When boiled, the filtrate evaporates without the appearance of any residue."
